    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4241\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in\nrelation to fees for the registration or reregistration of an\nagricultural trailer\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nTo provide a separate registration for agricultural trailers\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends paragraph (a) of subdivision 8 of section 401 of\nthe vehicle and traffic law to allow for registration of an\nagricultural trailer. This amendment provides restrictions for\nagricultural trailers that are similar to those for agricultural\ntrucks. The registration fee would be set at half the cost of a\nregular trailer.\n\nSection two is the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nRegistered agricultural trucks are only allowed on public highways\nwhen being used for the planting, cultivation and harvesting of\nagricultural, vegetable and food products; the raising, feeding and\ncare of livestock, bees, and poultry; or dairy farming. Individuals\nwho register their agricultural trucks pay a smaller fee than those\nwho register other types of trucks. However, there is no similar\ndistinction for registration between trailers that are used only for\nagricultural purposes and those trailers that are used for other\npurposes. Individuals who use their trailers in a manner similar to\nthe use of agricultural trucks must pay the full registration fee,\ndespite their limited agricultural use.\n\nRequiring farmers to pay the full registration fee for trailers that\nare only used for limited agricultural activities is inconsistent with\nthe existing statute providing a reduced fee for other types of\nagricultural vehicles. This bill seeks to remedy that inconsistency.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
