    "lawCode": "Amd §401, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4241B\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in\nrelation to fees for the registration or reregistration of an\nagricultural trailer\n\nPURPOSE: To provide a separate registration for agricultural trailers\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends schedule E of subdivision 7 of section 401 of the\nvehicle and traffic law: Paragraph one establishes an annual fee of\ntwo dollars and fifty-one cents for each five hundred pounds maximum\ngross weight, or fraction thereof, for each agricultural truck and\nagricultural trailer. Paragraph two defines \"agricultural truck\" and\n\"agricultural trailer\" for the purposes of this schedule. Paragraph\nthree declares that an agricultural truck and/or agricultural trailer\nshall be operated on the public highways only for the purposes set\nforth in paragraph two of this schedule. Paragraph four allows an\nagricultural trailer, in addition to an agricultural truck, to be\nregistered or reregistered for periods of less than one calendar year,\nwith the annual fees as provided in this schedule reduced\nproportionately on a monthly computation basis.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  Registered agricultural trucks are only allowed on\npublic highways when being used for the planting, cultivation and\nharvesting of agricultural, vegetable and food products; the raising,\nfeeding and care of livestock, bees, and poultry; or dairy farming.\nIndividuals who register their agricultural trucks pay a smaller fee\nthan those who register other types of trucks. However, there is no\nsimilar distinction for registration between trailers that are used\nonly for agricultural purposes and those trailers that are used for\nother purposes. Individuals who use their trailers in a manner similar\nto the use of agricultural trucks must pay the full registration fee,\ndespite their limited agricultural use.\n\nRequiring farmers to pay the full registration fee for trailers that\nare only used for limited agricultural activities is inconsistent with\nthe existing statute providing a reduced fee for other types of\nagricultural vehicles. This bill seeks to remedy that inconsistency.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY: New bill\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: To be determined\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:  This act shall take effect on the 90th day.\n\n",
